# Generative-mirror cross-platform stability (see sync_codex_mirror.py).
#
# Force LF in the working tree for BOTH the canonical skills and the generated
# .codex mirror so the drift-check (`sync_codex_mirror.py --check`) is byte-stable
# under core.autocrlf=true. Without this, autocrlf rewrites freshly checked-out
# .codex text files to CRLF while unchanged .claude files stay LF, producing a
# phantom "mirror STALE" that hard-fails every Codex-side gate after a merge/pull.
#
# text=auto leaves binary assets (png/woff/ttf/jpg/…) untouched.
.claude/skills/** text=auto eol=lf
.codex/skills/**  text=auto eol=lf
